cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use rocq-linlog in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: rocq-linlog
abstract: >-
  The Rocq library of linlog, a linear logic suite: the one-sided sequent
  calculus of linear logic with Mix, weakening and cut as parameters, the
  two-sided calculus of intuitionistic linear logic and its affine
  variant, and their first-order versions, as inductives; linlog's proof
  terms as datatypes, their checkers as functions and the theorems that a
  term a checker accepts proves its sequent, against which the
  certificates linlog writes are checked; the invariants every
  derivation keeps, which give certificates that a sequent is not
  derivable; and the reduction of Mix to ?(⊥⊗⊥). Its definitions,
  proofs, tests and documentation were written with substantial AI
  assistance, by Anthropic's Claude models in Claude Code, in steps the
  author planned, directed and accepted, and the author is responsible
  for them. Rocq's kernel checks every proof, and no theorem rests on an
  axiom: each one's assumptions are closed under the global context.
